    <region left="378" top="774" width="385" height="293" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="380" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>Bike USB powers micro:bit USB.<br />DG412 S1, V-, GND are soldered onto GND pads.<br />DG412 S4 is soldered onto P20.<br />DG412 D4, IN4 are soldered onto +3V3 pads.<br />DG412 S2 is patched with yellow wire onto nearest P2 pad.<br />DG412 VL is patched with red wire onto nearest +3V3 pad.<br />DG412 S3 is patched with orange wire onto nearest P1 pad.<br />Pin 1 purple GROUND is soldered and patched to GND.<br />Pin 2 blue BRAKE +10V is patched to DG412 IN2, V+, IN3.<br />Pin 3 green MOTOR DATA is soldered onto a P15 pad.<br />Pin 4 yellow HORN is patched to DG412 D2.<br />Pin 5 orange CONTROL DATA is soldered onto a P13 pad.<br />Pin 6 red BRAKE LIGHTS is patched to DG412 D3.<br /><br />Operation: <br />1. Switch on usb with steering arm raised to activate alarm.<br />2. Switch on usb with steering arm lowered for silent operation.<br />3. (De-)Accelerate to activate brake lights.<br />4. The B button adjusts the G-force needed.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
  </regions>
</worksheet>